{
 "title": "Geometry nodes 10: a sci-fi corridor",
 "summary": "An L-shaped corridor from a cube (extruded along Y and X, loop cuts for bays) dressed by geometry nodes: Separate Geometry picks the floor by its normal, and Subdivide Mesh, Triangulate and Dual Mesh (keep boundaries) turn it into hexagons, loosened with Split Edges and Scale Elements and thickened with Extrude Mesh over a plain floor; the walls and ceiling get inset panels (Extrude at 0, Scale Elements on the Top, extrude again) and a voronoi panel material; ceiling lights (an inset emissive cube) on the ceiling faces through Mesh to Points; pillars on the floor's points; point lights of different colours along it. Beyond the tutorial: a keyframed fly-through round the corner (the tutor records one with walk navigation).",
 "objects": [
  {
   "name": "Corridor",
   "description": "the corridor"
  }
 ],
